                <pb facs="0938" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v24/pg914"/>

                <head>433. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Laos<anchor n="0" xml:id="d433-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-11-09T16:50:00-05:00">November 9, 1962,
                            4:50 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>502. For Ambassadors Unger and Young. Laos situation reviewed at meeting with
                    the President Nov. 8.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d433-f2"/> Lao internal politics
                    discussed together with US assistance programs. It was emphasized that our
                    efforts are and will continue to be directed toward full support of Souvanna but if coalition fails we must try to
                    assure Souvanna and true neutrals will be
                    on our side and responsibility for collapse Geneva Agreements clearly on PL. President does not understand how arrest
                    incident could have occurred and desires Amb Unger continue to emphasize to Phoumi that he must sincerely and practically cooperate with
                        Souvanna to assure a wide
                    non-communist front, not just the Phoumi
                    Savannakhet faction. Phoumi must
                    understand that if a break-up of coalition does occur U.S. and international
                    opinion will hold him responsible if Souvanna has not been adequately supported by Phoumi’s faction.
                    If break occurs U.S. could not support Phoumi alone. Particularly disturbed that Phoumi unwilling to work with French military.
                    Is Phoumi preventing French technicians
                    sent out to replace ECCOIL from being used?</p>
                <p>To what extent are you in contact with neutralists in Vientiane in effort
                    convince them of need to resist PL pressures and
                    work for non-communist objectives of independence? Do you need additional
                    assistance for such purposes? (see septel concerning assistance to neutralist
                    military forces<anchor n="2" xml:id="d433-f3"/>).</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">For Bangkok:</hi> Desire that Amb Young take appropriate opportunity to emphasize
                    again to Sarit for him to continue to
                    counsel Phoumi to cooperate with Souvanna.
                        Sarit’s influence with Phoumi is indispensable in this respect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
